children.doc:
Multirotor flight with physics-verified dynamics (#335).

The chain, in the order a flight runs it:

* :mod:`.rotor` -- the propeller, from blade element momentum theory: thrust, torque and the figure of merit;
* :mod:`.model` -- the 6-DoF airframe: four rotors, the pack that sags, drag, ground effect, motor lag and the mixer;
* :mod:`.control` -- the cascade that flies it, which is never told about a fault;
* :mod:`.faults` -- the eight faults, injected where they physically act;
* :mod:`.residuals` -- the sensors, and Newton-Euler on the nominal vehicle against them;
* :mod:`.detect` -- three detectors tuned to the same false-alarm budget, and the diagnosis that reads the direction;
* :mod:`.sim` -- one flight, and the campaign over faults and seeds.

Compare ensembles on a stream of multiscale queries: scale-blind against scale-aware selection, with and without
closure / consistency checks and scale-linking models.

* :func:`evaluate_experts`: run every expert once per query (its raw output on the common grid, with the filter it
  carries), time it, and run the label-free checks that need its internals (an LES's closure health on its own
  grid, a scale-conditioned model's cross-scale self-consistency); the table is cached in an ``.npz`` file;
* :func:`adapt_output`: bring a raw output to the requested filter, blindly (apply the requested filter on top of
  whatever the output already carries) or scale-aware (:func:`~.filters.refilter`, only what is realizable);
* :func:`raw_residual` / :func:`closed_multiscale_residual`: label-free residuals of a predicted pair of snapshots,
  at the grid scale or of the filtered equations with the subfilter term removed;
* :func:`run_ensembles`: one :class:`~pinneapple_physics.ensemble.PhysicsEnsemble` per configuration on the same
  stream, replaying the cached outputs;
* :func:`summarise_runs`, :func:`closure_flag_table`, :func:`markdown_tables`, :func:`summary_figure`.

functions.doc:
Errors at each width (``widths`` in units of ``bench.h``) on the cases ``idx``:

* ``conditioned(w0, nu, delta)``: the scale-conditioned model asked at ``delta``;
* ``fixed``: ``{width: predict(w0, nu)}``, models trained at one width; evaluated at ``delta`` by post-filtering
  the narrowest one at or below ``delta`` (exact for Gaussians), the best of them reported;
* ``blind(w0, nu, delta)``: the same network without the width input (its input is still filtered at ``delta``);

plus the spectrum error of the conditioned model and its self-consistency (prediction at ``delta``, filtered to
``2 delta``, against the prediction at ``2 delta``).

The paper's four coupling classes as sympy laws in the module's symbols (``_symbols()``), one tuple
``(key, title, b_ab, b_ba)`` each (``b_ba`` None: reciprocal), ready for :func:`analyze_ep_tuning`:

* ``reciprocal_linear``: b = J + c lam (the no-go case, ``c`` a free complex symbol);
* ``phase_only``: b = J exp(i lam) (the EP does not move);
* ``route_a``: b = sqrt(J^2 + lam J G) (exact, PT symmetric);
* ``route_c``: b_ab = J, b_ba = J + lam G (exact, non-reciprocal).

